# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .prettierignore — files Prettier must NEVER reformat.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES
#   Anything matched here is skipped by Prettier, both when you run
#   `npx prettier --write .` by hand and when the Claude Code auto-format hook
#   (.claude/settings.json) fires after an edit.
#
# WHEN IT RUNS
#   Every time Prettier runs. It is read automatically — no flag needed.
#
# HOW TO USE IT
#   Add one glob pattern per line (same syntax as .gitignore) for anything that
#   is machine-generated, downloaded, or where formatting would cause harm.
#
# WHY THESE ENTRIES
#   Generated code (Prisma client, .next build output) is overwritten on every
#   build, so formatting it is wasted work and creates noisy diffs. Lockfiles
#   are managed by npm and must stay byte-for-byte as npm wrote them.
#
# This file is tooling only. It has no effect on the running application.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# dependencies and build output
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage
.vercel

# generated code — regenerated by `prisma generate`, never hand-edited
lib/generated
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# package manager lockfiles — owned by npm
package-lock.json

# environment files (secrets; also gitignored)
.env*
